1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,651
Welcome to Unit Two of Algebra One, where
we start solving equations.

2
00:00:05,101 --> 00:00:09,837
In this lesson, we'll solve one-step
equations, and learn the one rule that

3
00:00:09,837 --> 00:00:11,479
makes every equation work.

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:17,528
An equation says two things are equal. You
can picture it as a balanced scale.

5
00:00:17,978 --> 00:00:21,626
Here, x plus three on the left balances
seven on the right.

6
00:00:22,076 --> 00:00:27,553
If you take three away from the left side
only, the scale tips. To keep it balanced,

7
00:00:27,553 --> 00:00:30,161
take three away from the right side too.

8
00:00:30,611 --> 00:00:35,374
That's the golden rule of equations:
whatever you do to one side, do to the

9
00:00:35,374 --> 00:00:36,073
other side.

10
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:43,240
To solve, we want x alone on one side. We
undo whatever is being done to x, using

11
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,880
the inverse operation.

12
00:00:45,330 --> 00:00:50,961
Addition and subtraction undo each other.
Multiplication and division undo each

13
00:00:50,961 --> 00:00:51,389
other.

14
00:00:51,839 --> 00:00:57,936
In x plus three equals seven, three is
added to x. So we subtract three from both

15
00:00:57,936 --> 00:00:58,388
sides.

16
00:00:58,838 --> 00:01:04,812
x plus three minus three is just x, and
seven minus three is four. So x equals

17
00:01:04,812 --> 00:01:05,195
four.

18
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:10,643
Always check your answer by putting it
back into the original equation.

19
00:01:11,093 --> 00:01:16,383
Four plus three is seven. Seven equals
seven, so x equals four is correct.

20
00:01:17,533 --> 00:01:23,793
Now x minus five equals two. Five is
subtracted from x, so we add five to both

21
00:01:23,793 --> 00:01:24,275
sides.

22
00:01:24,725 --> 00:01:30,613
x minus five plus five is x, and two plus
five is seven. So x equals seven.

23
00:01:31,733 --> 00:01:37,558
Next, four x equals twenty. Here x is
multiplied by four, so we divide both

24
00:01:37,558 --> 00:01:38,645
sides by four.

25
00:01:39,095 --> 00:01:46,093
Four x divided by four is x, and twenty
divided by four is five. So x equals five.

26
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:54,032
Finally, x divided by three equals six. x
is divided by three, so we multiply both

27
00:01:54,032 --> 00:01:55,276
sides by three.

28
00:01:55,726 --> 00:02:02,019
x over three, times three, is x. Six times
three is eighteen. So x equals eighteen.

29
00:02:02,469 --> 00:02:05,499
Check: eighteen divided by three is six.
It works.

30
00:02:06,633 --> 00:02:09,897
Your turn. Solve negative three x equals
twelve.

31
00:02:10,347 --> 00:02:11,883
Pause the video and try it.

32
00:02:12,333 --> 00:02:17,795
x is multiplied by negative three, so
divide both sides by negative three.

33
00:02:18,245 --> 00:02:24,026
Twelve divided by negative three is
negative four. So x equals negative four.

34
00:02:24,476 --> 00:02:28,423
Check: negative three times negative four
is twelve. Correct.

35
00:02:29,566 --> 00:02:34,942
Some equations need two steps to solve,
like three x plus five equals twenty.

36
00:02:35,392 --> 00:02:38,784
In this lesson, we'll learn which step to
do first, and why.

37
00:02:39,933 --> 00:02:45,565
To build three x plus five, you start with
x, multiply by three, then add five.

38
00:02:46,015 --> 00:02:51,686
To solve, we undo those steps in reverse
order. First undo the adding, then undo

39
00:02:51,686 --> 00:02:52,820
the multiplying.

40
00:02:53,270 --> 00:02:57,922
It's like getting dressed. You put on
socks, then shoes. To undress, the shoes

41
00:02:57,922 --> 00:02:58,817
come off first.

42
00:02:59,966 --> 00:03:02,825
Let's solve three x plus five equals
twenty.

43
00:03:03,275 --> 00:03:08,181
First, subtract five from both sides. That
gives three x equals fifteen.

44
00:03:08,631 --> 00:03:12,194
Then divide both sides by three. x equals
five.

45
00:03:12,644 --> 00:03:16,121
Check: three times five, plus five, is
twenty. It works.

46
00:03:17,266 --> 00:03:20,125
Next, x over four, minus two, equals
three.

47
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:24,521
First add two to both sides, so x over
four equals five.

48
00:03:24,971 --> 00:03:28,790
Then multiply both sides by four. x equals
twenty.

49
00:03:29,933 --> 00:03:33,559
Watch the signs in seven minus two x
equals fifteen.

50
00:03:34,009 --> 00:03:38,937
Subtract seven from both sides. That
leaves negative two x equals eight.

51
00:03:39,387 --> 00:03:43,910
Divide both sides by negative two, and x
equals negative four.

52
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:49,629
Check: seven minus two times negative four
is seven plus eight, which is fifteen.

53
00:03:50,766 --> 00:03:56,079
One exception. In the quantity x plus
four, all over three, equals five, the

54
00:03:56,079 --> 00:03:58,595
whole left side is divided by three.

55
00:03:59,045 --> 00:04:04,514
So this time we multiply both sides by
three first, to get x plus four equals

56
00:04:04,514 --> 00:04:05,083
fifteen.

57
00:04:05,533 --> 00:04:08,242
Then subtract four, and x equals eleven.

58
00:04:09,366 --> 00:04:13,163
Your turn. Solve five x minus eight equals
seventeen.

59
00:04:13,613 --> 00:04:15,149
Pause the video and try it.

60
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:19,226
Add eight to both sides, so five x equals
twenty-five.

61
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:23,047
Divide both sides by five, and x equals
five.

62
00:04:23,497 --> 00:04:27,187
Check: five times five minus eight is
seventeen. Correct.

63
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:33,154
Real equations often take several steps,
and can have x on both sides.

64
00:04:33,604 --> 00:04:37,252
In this lesson, we'll use a simple plan
that solves them all.

65
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:42,026
Here's the plan. First, distribute to
clear any parentheses.

66
00:04:42,476 --> 00:04:44,887
Second, combine like terms on each side.

67
00:04:45,337 --> 00:04:49,710
Third, if x appears on both sides, move
the x terms to one side.

68
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:55,801
Then finish like a two-step equation: undo
adding or subtracting, then undo

69
00:04:55,801 --> 00:04:57,606
multiplying or dividing.

70
00:04:58,733 --> 00:05:03,789
Let's solve two times the quantity x plus
three, plus four, equals eighteen.

71
00:05:04,239 --> 00:05:08,378
Distribute the two: two x plus six, plus
four, equals eighteen.

72
00:05:08,828 --> 00:05:12,220
Combine like terms: two x plus ten equals
eighteen.

73
00:05:12,670 --> 00:05:18,932
Subtract ten from both sides, to get two x
equals eight. Divide by two, and x equals

74
00:05:18,932 --> 00:05:19,304
four.

75
00:05:20,433 --> 00:05:24,465
Next, five x minus two plus three x equals
forty-six.

76
00:05:24,915 --> 00:05:30,056
Combine five x and three x, to get eight x
minus two equals forty-six.

77
00:05:30,506 --> 00:05:35,221
Add two to both sides: eight x equals
forty-eight. So x equals six.

78
00:05:36,366 --> 00:05:41,614
Now x is on both sides: five x plus three
equals two x plus eighteen.

79
00:05:42,064 --> 00:05:47,857
Subtract two x from both sides, so the x
terms are together on the left. That gives

80
00:05:47,857 --> 00:05:50,299
three x plus three equals eighteen.

81
00:05:50,749 --> 00:05:55,933
Subtract three: three x equals fifteen.
Divide by three: x equals five.

82
00:05:57,066 --> 00:06:02,101
A useful tip: move the smaller x term, so
you avoid a negative coefficient.

83
00:06:02,551 --> 00:06:08,759
In four x minus seven equals nine x plus
eight, subtract four x from both sides.

84
00:06:09,209 --> 00:06:12,430
That gives negative seven equals five x
plus eight.

85
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:18,342
Subtract eight: negative fifteen equals
five x. So x equals negative three.

86
00:06:18,792 --> 00:06:21,693
Check: both sides come out to negative
nineteen.

87
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:28,725
Let's use the whole plan on three times
the quantity x minus four, equals x plus

88
00:06:28,725 --> 00:06:29,020
six.

89
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:33,075
Distribute: three x minus twelve equals x
plus six.

90
00:06:33,525 --> 00:06:37,792
Subtract x from both sides: two x minus
twelve equals six.

91
00:06:38,242 --> 00:06:41,932
Add twelve: two x equals eighteen. So x
equals nine.

92
00:06:43,066 --> 00:06:48,555
Your turn. Solve two times the quantity
three x plus one, equals four x plus

93
00:06:48,555 --> 00:06:49,061
twelve.

94
00:06:49,511 --> 00:06:51,047
Pause the video and try it.

95
00:06:51,497 --> 00:06:55,422
Distribute: six x plus two equals four x
plus twelve.

96
00:06:55,872 --> 00:07:02,230
Subtract four x: two x plus two equals
twelve. Subtract two: two x equals ten.

97
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:06,562
So x equals five. Check: both sides equal
thirty-two.

98
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:13,198
Most equations have exactly one solution.
But some have none at all, and some have

99
00:07:13,198 --> 00:07:14,271
infinitely many.

100
00:07:14,721 --> 00:07:17,622
In this lesson, we'll learn how to tell
which is which.

101
00:07:18,767 --> 00:07:22,308
First, the usual case. Two x plus one
equals seven.

102
00:07:22,758 --> 00:07:28,478
Subtract one, then divide by two, and x
equals three. Exactly one number works.

103
00:07:28,478 --> 00:07:29,926
That's one solution.

104
00:07:31,067 --> 00:07:34,843
Now try three x plus five equals three x
minus two.

105
00:07:35,293 --> 00:07:40,845
Subtract three x from both sides. The x
terms cancel, and we're left with five

106
00:07:40,845 --> 00:07:42,269
equals negative two.

107
00:07:42,719 --> 00:07:48,549
That's false. Five never equals negative
two, no matter what x is. So this equation

108
00:07:48,549 --> 00:07:49,673
has no solution.

109
00:07:50,123 --> 00:07:54,861
On a graph, the two sides are parallel
lines. They have the same slope, so they

110
00:07:54,861 --> 00:07:55,521
never meet.

111
00:07:56,667 --> 00:08:01,232
Next, two times the quantity x plus three,
equals two x plus six.

112
00:08:01,682 --> 00:08:05,266
Distribute: two x plus six equals two x
plus six.

113
00:08:05,716 --> 00:08:11,199
Subtract two x from both sides, and we get
six equals six. That's always true.

114
00:08:11,649 --> 00:08:16,818
Every value of x works, so there are
infinitely many solutions. The two sides

115
00:08:16,818 --> 00:08:18,497
are really the same line.

116
00:08:19,633 --> 00:08:24,540
Here's the rule. Simplify until the x
terms are gone, or you have x alone.

117
00:08:24,990 --> 00:08:27,123
If x is left, there's one solution.

118
00:08:27,573 --> 00:08:31,584
If x disappears and the statement is
false, there's no solution.

119
00:08:32,034 --> 00:08:37,623
If x disappears and the statement is true,
there are infinitely many solutions, all

120
00:08:37,623 --> 00:08:38,498
real numbers.

121
00:08:39,633 --> 00:08:45,243
Let's try one more. Five times the
quantity x minus one, equals five x plus

122
00:08:45,243 --> 00:08:45,543
one.

123
00:08:45,993 --> 00:08:50,089
Distribute: five x minus five equals five
x plus one.

124
00:08:50,539 --> 00:08:56,000
Subtract five x: negative five equals one.
That's false, so there's no solution.

125
00:08:57,133 --> 00:09:02,573
Your turn. Solve three times the quantity
x plus two, equals three x plus six.

126
00:09:03,023 --> 00:09:04,559
Pause the video and try it.

127
00:09:05,009 --> 00:09:08,764
Distribute: three x plus six equals three
x plus six.

128
00:09:09,214 --> 00:09:14,296
Subtract three x: six equals six. That's
true, so there are infinitely many

129
00:09:14,296 --> 00:09:14,974
solutions.

130
00:09:16,100 --> 00:09:21,633
Next time, we'll solve literal equations
and formulas. If this helped, subscribe to

131
00:09:21,633 --> 00:09:26,633
School Math, Explained, and turn on
notifications so you don't miss it. See

132
00:09:26,633 --> 00:09:27,300
you there.

